
---------------------------------------------------------------
  Wzonka-Lad - Yet Another Gameboy Emulator for 68020+ Amigas  
---------------------------------------------------------------
           Written by Ville Helin in 1996-1999
 For the latest sources: https://github.com/vhelin/wzonka-lad


1. BACKGROUND

This is a Gameboy emulator written completely in 68020 asm.
This used to be shareware, but it is now (after 11-Aug-2003)
GPL 2 software.


2. LEGAL STUFF

Wzonka-Lad is GPL 2 software. Read the LICENSE file for
further information. You use Wzonka-Lad at your own risk.
I take no responsibility for anything.


2. CHANGELOG (RECENT)

v1.13.00 (28-Nov-2026):

* Overlapping sprites now follow DMG priority in all graphics modes:
  the leftmost sprite wins, with earlier OAM entries breaking ties.
  A winning sprite with the behind-background flag set is hidden by
  nonzero background or window pixels, but still blocks other sprites.
* The Palette Editor can reset background and sprite colours independently
  to their built-in defaults.
* The Palette Editor now replies to GadTools events correctly and ignores
  mouse moves that did not come from a colour slider.
* Copying a colour onto an identical RGB value no longer reallocates a
  Workbench pen or redraws the Palette Editor previews.
* Visual settings can restore the emulator's built-in background and
  sprite colours with the Reset button in the Colours box.
* The Visual settings colour preview now decodes its artwork without Chip
  RAM and uses the appropriate drawing path for native or RTG Workbench
  screens. True-colour RTG previews show the palette's RGB values directly.
* FULL and FAST skip the timer IRQ deadline calculation when TIMA
  cannot reload in the current CPU slice, preserving exact timing.
* FAST and WARP now mirror interrupt stack writes into Echo RAM and
  handle pushes that cross a memory boundary. LDH reads of STAT sample
  the LCD mode at the read cycle. WARP also requests STAT on a new
  LY=LYC match when the LCD is turned on, without periodic STAT updates.
* OAM DMA copies all 160 bytes unchanged, including the low four bits of
  each sprite attribute byte. $FF46 remembers the last byte written.
* Pending IRQs raised by guest I/O writes are checked before fetching
  the next instruction, including HALT.
* FAST and WARP now use 114 M-cycles per normal scanline, a cycle-based
  divider, and five M-cycles for interrupt entry. FAST TIMA uses divider
  edges and preserves writes and post-overflow ticks. WARP still omits
  periodic TIMA updates.
* MBC5 RAM header codes $04 and $05 now support all 128 KiB and 64 KiB,
  respectively, including battery saves and snapshots. Last Crown Warriors
  uses the 128 KiB layout.
* VBlank, serial completion, FAST timer overflow, and WARP LYC writes
  now latch their interrupt requests even if IE masks them. WARP also
  dispatches pending STAT and timer interrupts to the correct vectors.
* Joypad register P1 ($FF00) now reads bits 7-6 as ones after writes and
  snapshot loads.
* FAST and WARP now wrap taken relative jumps below $0000 into high RAM
  without adding a check to ordinary opcode fetches. Quartet uses this.
* FULL and FAST no longer suppress HBlank STAT after the LYC interrupt
  source is disabled or LY stops matching LYC.
* FULL and FAST now compare LY with LYC throughout VBlank. This restores
  the line-150 STAT interrupt used by the Chantey demo.
* With the LCD off, LY and the STAT mode stay at zero and the inactive
  modes no longer request STAT interrupts. Turning the LCD back on
  restarts the scanline counter and checks LYC against line zero without
  raising a new STAT interrupt if the previous match is still true.
* Pending VBlank and STAT interrupts are now serviced even after the LCD
  is turned off, so they no longer block lower-priority interrupts.
* DMG serial control ($FF02) now reads bits 1-6 as ones, as on hardware.
  This lets FULL pass Rhythm Land's serial register check.
* Fixed MBC5 ROM bank layout: games start in bank 1 and can explicitly
  select bank 0 at $4000. This fixes Rhythm Land's blank screen.
* Fixed upper ROM bank selection in the $4000-$7FFF window for 1 and 2 MiB
  MBC1 cartridges, allowing Sam Mallard to boot.
